---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | SatvaStones Fine Anti-Tarnish Jewellery"
  description="Official Privacy Policy compliant with the Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023, DPDP Rules 2025, and Information Technology Act 2000. Data fiduciary: Anirudh A Verma."
>
  <!-- Minimalist Legal Header -->
  <div class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="max-w-[1240px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center space-y-2">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 bg-rose-50 border border-rose-200 rounded-full text-xs font-bold text-[#a1505a]">
        <span>Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 Compliant</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Data Fiduciary:</strong> Anirudh A Verma (Sole Proprietor of SatvaStones Jewellery) • GSTIN: 24DDAPV4074H1ZF • Registered Atelier: Chala, Vapi, Gujarat - 396191, India.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-gray-400">
        Effective Date: 1st March 2026 | Policy Version: 2026.1-DPDP | Last Reviewed: November 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-[1240px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 sm:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10 bg-white p-6 sm:p-12 border border-gray-200 rounded-[26px] shadow-xs text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">

      <!-- Executive Overview -->
      <section class="space-y-3 bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-gray-200">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-900 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#f2707f]"></span>
          <span>1. Legislative Scope & Commitment</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          SatvaStones Fine Jewellery ("SatvaStones", "we", "our", or "us") operates the e-commerce storefront <strong>www.satvastones.in</strong> (and <strong>satvastones.in</strong>). We are committed to safeguarding the digital personal data of our patrons ("Data Principals") in strict accordance with:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 pl-2 text-gray-600">
          <li><strong>The Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act)</strong> and the <strong>DPDP Rules, 2025</strong>;</li>
          <li><strong>The Information Technology Act, 2000</strong> and the <strong>IT (Reasonable Security Practices and Procedures and Sensitive Personal Data or Information) Rules, 2011 (SPDI Rules)</strong>; and</li>
          <li><strong>The Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules, 2020</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We act as the <strong>Data Fiduciary</strong>. We do not sell, rent, monetize, or trade your personal data to any data broker or commercial advertiser.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Itemized Data Collection & Purpose -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
          2. Personal Data We Collect & Specific Grounds of Processing
        </h2>
        <p>
          Under Section 6 of the DPDP Act 2023, personal data is processed solely for specified, lawful, and necessary purposes on the basis of your explicit, affirmative consent or legitimate statutory uses:
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-gray-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <thead class="bg-gray-100 text-gray-800 font-bold uppercase text-[10px] tracking-wider">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200">Personal Data Element</th>
                <th class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200">Specified Business Purpose</th>
                <th class="p-3 border-b border-gray-200">Legal Ground (DPDP Act)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Full Name, Phone Number, Delivery Address</td>
                <td class="p-3">Order dispatch from Vapi atelier, AWB generation, doorstep courier handover, and delivery SMS updates.</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-800 font-medium">Contract Performance & Consent</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Email Address</td>
                <td class="p-3">Issuance of statutory GST Tax Invoices, tracking link dispatch, and customer support communications.</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-800 font-medium">Legal Obligation (CGST Act) & Consent</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">Payment Transaction ID & Gateway Token</td>
                <td class="p-3">Authorization of payments via RBI-licensed gateway (Razorpay). <em>Note: Card numbers, CVV, and UPI MPIN are never handled or stored on our servers.</em></td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-800 font-medium">Contract Performance & Payment Security</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">360° Unboxing Video Footage</td>
                <td class="p-3">Verification of transit damage or missing item claims for free replacement dispatch from Vapi.</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-800 font-medium">Explicit Consent / Warranty Verification</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-gray-900">IP Address, Device Type & Consent Timestamp</td>
                <td class="p-3">Fraud detection, DDoS mitigation via Cloudflare Edge, and mandatory DPDP Rule 4 consent logging.</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-800 font-medium">Security & Statutory Audit Compliance</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Third-Party Processors -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
          3. Authorized Data Processors & Sub-Processors
        </h2>
        <p>
          We engage certified Data Processors under strict Data Processing Agreements ensuring equal or higher data protection standards:
        </p>
        <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 pt-2">
          <li class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block">Razorpay Software Pvt. Ltd.</strong>
            <span class="text-gray-600 text-[11px]">Payment Gateway (RBI regulated, PCI-DSS Level 1 certified). Processes UPI, Credit/Debit Cards, and NetBanking.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block">BlueDart Express & Delhivery Prime</strong>
            <span class="text-gray-600 text-[11px]">Logistics Partners. Receives shipping address and phone number strictly for domestic delivery execution.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block">Cloudflare, Inc.</strong>
            <span class="text-gray-600 text-[11px]">Edge Hosting, Cloudflare D1 database, and R2 storage with edge nodes in India (Mumbai, Chennai, Delhi, Bengaluru, Hyderabad).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="p-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-200">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block">Cloudinary Ltd.</strong>
            <span class="text-gray-600 text-[11px]">Secure media CDN hosting product catalog photography and optimized digital assets.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Data Retention Schedule -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
          4. Statutory Data Retention Schedule
        </h2>
        <p>
          In accordance with Section 8(7) of the DPDP Act 2023 and prevailing Indian financial statutes:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pl-2">
          <li><strong>GST Tax Invoices & Order Records:</strong> Retained for a mandatory period of <strong>8 years</strong> as required under Section 36 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act, 2017 (CGST Act) and Indian taxation laws.</li>
          <li><strong>DPDP Consent Logs & Access Audit Trails:</strong> Retained for a minimum of <strong>1 year</strong> in compliance with Rule 6 of the Digital Personal Data Protection Rules, 2025.</li>
          <li><strong>Promotional / Marketing Identifiers:</strong> Erased or anonymized <strong>immediately</strong> upon your withdrawal of consent.</li>
          <li><strong>360° Unboxing Claim Videos:</strong> Retained for <strong>90 days</strong> post-resolution of the replacement claim, then securely purged from our Cloudflare R2 storage.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Security Measures -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
          5. Reasonable Security Practices & Safeguards
        </h2>
        <p>
          Pursuant to Section 8(5) of the DPDP Act 2023 and Rule 5 of the SPDI Rules 2011, we implement robust technical safeguards:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 pl-2">
          <li><strong>Transport Layer Security:</strong> All client-to-server traffic is encrypted using TLS 1.3 / HTTPS with HSTS preloading.</li>
          <li><strong>Database Encryption:</strong> Stored data in Cloudflare D1 and R2 is encrypted at rest using AES-256.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Card Data Retention:</strong> We never capture or store raw card numbers, PINs, or CVVs. All payment transactions occur directly within Razorpay's PCI-DSS Level 1 tokenized iframe.</li>
          <li><strong>Granular Role Access:</strong> Administrative panel access is restricted via encrypted cryptographic tokens and two-step verification.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Rights of Data Principals -->
      <section class="space-y-4 bg-rose-50/40 p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl border border-rose-200">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-gray-900">
          6. Your Statutory Rights Under the DPDP Act, 2023
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs">
          As a Data Principal, you are entitled to exercise the following rights directly via our self-serve <a href="/privacy-rights" class="text-[#a1505a] font-bold underline">Privacy Rights Portal</a>:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-rose-100">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block mb-1">A. Right to Access (Section 11)</strong>
            <span>Obtain a summary of personal data being processed and identities of all Data Processors who received your data.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-rose-100">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block mb-1">B. Right to Correction & Updation (Section 12)</strong>
            <span>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete shipping addresses, phone numbers, or profile information.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-rose-100">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block mb-1">C. Right to Erasure / "To Be Forgotten"</strong>
            <span>Request deletion of personal data no longer necessary for the original purpose (subject to mandatory 8-year GST tax invoice laws).</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-rose-100">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block mb-1">D. Right to Withdraw Consent</strong>
            <span>Revoke marketing or non-essential cookie consent at any time with 1 click without affecting prior lawful processing.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-rose-100 sm:col-span-2">
            <strong class="text-gray-900 block mb-1">E. Right to Nominate (Section 14)</strong>
            <span>Nominate any designated individual who shall exercise your data rights in the unfortunate event of death or incapacity.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Protection of Children -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-100 pb-2">
          7. Protection of Children & Minors (Section 9)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our services and fine jewellery collections are intended exclusively for individuals aged <strong>18 years and above</strong> who possess legal capacity to enter into binding contracts under the Indian Contract Act, 1872. We do not knowingly collect, process, or track personal data of minors, nor do we engage in targeted behavioral advertising directed at children. If you believe a minor has provided us with personal data without verifiable parental consent, contact our Grievance Officer immediately for prompt erasure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Grievance Redressal Officer -->
      <section class="space-y-3 bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-gray-200">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900">
          8. Grievance Officer & Statutory Redressal Mechanism
        </h2>
        <p>
          In compliance with Rule 5(9) of the IT SPDI Rules 2011, the Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules 2020, and Section 13 of the DPDP Act 2023, our designated Grievance Officer is:
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-1 text-xs text-gray-800 bg-white p-4 rounded-xl border border-gray-200">
          <p><strong>Name:</strong> Anirudh A Verma</p>
          <p><strong>Designation:</strong> Grievance Officer & Proprietor</p>
          <p><strong>Entity Name:</strong> SatvaStones Jewellery</p>
          <p><strong>Physical Address:</strong> Chala, Vapi, Gujarat - 396191, India</p>
          <p><strong>Official Grievance Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:grievance@satvastones.in" class="text-[#f2707f] font-bold underline">grievance@satvastones.in</a> (CC: <a href="mailto:support@satvastones.in" class="text-[#f2707f] font-bold underline">support@satvastones.in</a>)</p>
          <p><strong>Customer Care Helpline / Call & WhatsApp:</strong> <a href="tel:+919016703180" class="text-[#f2707f] font-bold underline">+91 90167 03180</a> (Mon–Sat, 10:00 AM – 7:00 PM IST)</p>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 pt-1">
          <strong>Statutory SLA:</strong> All privacy grievances will be acknowledged within <strong>48 hours</strong> and resolved within <strong>1 month (30 days)</strong> from the date of receipt. If unresolved, you may lodge a complaint with the <strong>Data Protection Board of India (DPBI)</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
